heir money out but after Roosevelt  calmly explained what he was doing to  fix the problems in the banking system  and the banks reopened  suddenly there were lines of depositors  waiting to put their money back in  Roosevelt would make 27 more fireside  chats they remain a landmark in  presidential communication it is less  widely known that FDR had tried this  process out as early as 1929 while he  was governor of New York often asking  listeners directly for their help in  passing liberal legislation through a  conservative state legislature it is  even less widely admitted by Roosevelt's  admirers that what he was doing was  intentionally bypassing the mainstream  media  it cannot misrepresent nor misquote said  his press secretary Stephen early about  live radio it is far-reaching and  simultaneous in releasing messages given  it for transmission to the nation or for  international consumption it sound like  anybody we know  tweeting is like a typewriter when I put  it out you put it immediately on your  show so when somebody says something  about me I am able to go Bing Bing Bing  and I take care of it I can express my  views when somebody expresses maybe a  false view that they said I gave yes  he's an idiot and his quotes read like  somebody who just got hit on the head by  a low flying duck but in between the  inanity z' is an essential truth just  like Franklin Roosevelt Donald Trump  figured out how to bypass the  established media how to force it to  report only what topics he wanted it to  report how to get his quote exactly the  way he wanted it and how to at least  start if not utterly control the  narrative moreover just as sitting  around your home in 1933 hearing the  president addressing you just you or  just your family not an audience full of  people at a speech it was an utterly  novel and bonding experience how do you  read Twitter is it you as part of a  crowd do a bunch of your friends get  together and you all read the same  tweets or is it just you by yourself  reading what the people you follow have  written in essence to you how many times  do you confuse a tweet with a Twitter  direct message or even a text if you  love trumpet is easy to dismiss what he  does there asthma  you'll ative morally barren corrupt and  dishonest but two people in the cult  that's him  talking to them just them individually  one at a time the only practical  broadcasting knowledge I was ever taught  in college was by a professor who also  ran the radio stations that Cornell  University owned whenever I hear  somebody say hello world or good morning  Ithaca used to say I look around to see  if somebody's come into the room with me  communication is individual don't say  good evening everyone just say good  evening in almost every speech Barack  Obama would start with hello Chicago or  hello Phil in city name here or on  occasion hello America and I would  cringe amazingly for such a strong  speaker he never got this point people  don't want to hear a speech they want to  have a conversation even if you are the  only one talking at the moment  Trump presumably from his years as a con  man knowing that you rip people off not  in large groups but one at a time  recognize this in Twitter as long as he  has that access he will have core  support this was a metaphorical war for  his cult his election was to them what  Pearl Harbor was to Japan and he has  perfected the fireside tweet he may  truly have absolutely nothing of any  meaning to sell them but he can sell  something to them anyway you know he  added on the subject of Twitter you have  to keep people interested without social  media I'm not sure that I would be here  talking I would probably not be here  talking we can only guess if there was  an unconscious admission in there about  the Russian Facebook ads but we don't  have to guess about the larger point it  is painful to contemplate this but he is  the FDR  of Twitter resist remove piece so I  don't have to keep 